            "num:128.51GB"
          ],
          "narration": "gpt oss or G L M? File size decides. You've got one hundred twenty-eight gigabytes of unified memory, one shared pool, and a coding habit to feed tonight."
        },
        {
          "id": "s2",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 13.4,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:unified memory",
            "glossary:KV cache"
          ],
          "narration": "Unified memory means one pool. Your model weights live in it. So does the K V cache, the scratchpad that grows with every line of context. So does your operating system. The file has to fit with room left over, or nothing runs."
        },
        {
          "id": "s3",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 6.2,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:total vs active parameters"
          ],
          "narration": "Total parameters decide whether it fits. Active parameters decide how fast it thinks. The two numbers pull in opposite directions."
        },
        {
          "id": "s4",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 9.4,
          "specific": false,
          "hits": [],
          "narration": "It's a mixture of experts, a model that wakes a small slice of itself for each word. All of it sits in your memory. Only the slice does the thinking."
        },
        {
          "id": "s5",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 11.2,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "num:65GB"
          ],
          "narration": "Start with cost. Ollama ships gpt oss in exactly one quant, a single sixty-five-gigabyte download, and one command starts it. A quant is just a compression setting, fewer bits per weight. Sixty-five gigabytes leaves real headroom."
        },
        {
          "id": "s6",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 11.9,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "num:45.34 t/s"
          ],
          "narration": "Now speed, because fitting is not flying. The llama dot cpp maintainer measured this model on this exact class of hardware. It reads back at forty-five point three four tokens a second. That's typing speed, not waiting speed."
        },
        {
          "id": "s7",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 9.7,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:Q4_K_M",
            "entity:GLM-4.5",
            "entity:GLM-4.5-Air"
          ],
          "narration": "G L M four point five Air is the other survivor. Its recommended quant, the file the makers suggest, still fits with room to spare, and a richer quant fits too."
        },
        {
          "id": "s8",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 6.9,
          "specific": false,
          "hits": [],
          "narration": "Its decode speed here? Nobody has measured it on this hardware. What you get instead is more quality per gigabyte of memory."
        },
        {
          "id": "s9",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 10.0,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:SWE-bench Verified"
          ],
          "narration": "Now the honest catch. On the software engineering benchmark, a board built from real GitHub fixes, the open leaders score far above gpt oss. No page we found has measured them here."
        },
        {
          "id": "s10",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 7.2,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:GLM-4.5"
          ],
          "narration": "Those leaders are full-size models, G L M, Kimi, DeepSeek. Whether any of them fits your box at all, nobody has measured it."
        },
        {
          "id": "s11",
          "role": "payoff_close",
          "est_duration_s": 11.9,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:GLM-4.5",
